# LEADING SLASHES MATTER. These are gitignore-style patterns: a bare `work/`
# would match every directory of that name at any depth. Anchored to the
# project root, each pattern means only what it says.
#
# COMMENTS GO ON THEIR OWN LINE. A trailing comment becomes part of the
# pattern and the pattern then matches nothing; that is how the first smoke
# deploy shipped tools/, source/ and work/ to production for twenty minutes
# on 16 September 2026.

# the Python asset pipeline; never runs on Vercel
/tools/
# ElevenLabs generation; needs the key, never ships
/scripts/
# the authors' PDF and cover
/source/
# intermediates and contact sheets
/work/
# the HyperFrames composition and its renders
/reel/
/node_modules/
*.py
*.mjs
*.pdf
*.md
*.json.bak
__pycache__/
.env*
.vercel/
.vercelignore
.gitignore
# the landscape snapshot harness (junctions + a 1280x720 copy of the reel page)
/reel-landscape/
